PATCH: zephyr_ethernet_mcast_null_guard — don't deref a header-less pkt in L2
=============================================================================

Written against: Zephyr 4.4.x  (verified present in v4.4.1 and main, 2026-06)
Target platform: ESP32-S3 on Zephyr RTOS, Ethernet L2
Application:     /workspace/projects/hello_eink  (LLSS e-ink client)

SUMMARY
-------
ethernet_fill_header()'s multicast/broadcast destination helpers read
NET_IPV4_HDR(pkt)->dst / NET_IPV6_HDR(pkt)->dst with no check that the packet
has an IP header. net_pkt_ip_data() is `pkt->frags->data`, so a header-less pkt
(frags==NULL, e.g. when net_pkt allocation fails under TX-pool exhaustion)
causes a NULL-region load (observed EXCCAUSE 28 load-prohibited, VADDR 0x11) and
halts the kernel. This is the failure that turned a TX-pool drain into a fatal
crash.

ROOT CAUSE / FIX
----------------
Guard the three helpers (ethernet_ipv4_dst_is_broadcast_or_mcast,
ethernet_fill_in_dst_on_ipv4_mcast, ethernet_fill_in_dst_on_ipv6_mcast) with
net_pkt_is_empty(pkt) (short-circuits on !buffer) so a header-less pkt is
treated as not-bcast/mcast (falls through to the resolved L2 dst) instead of
dereferencing NULL. Robustness fix: a packet must never be able to halt the
kernel. Full writeup: NETBUF_LEAK_ADVENTURE.md.

--- 8< --- diff --- 8< ---
--- a/subsys/net/l2/ethernet/ethernet.c
+++ b/subsys/net/l2/ethernet/ethernet.c
@@ -464,6 +464,13 @@
 #if defined(CONFIG_NET_IPV4)
 static inline bool ethernet_ipv4_dst_is_broadcast_or_mcast(struct net_pkt *pkt)
 {
+	/* A header-less pkt (frags==NULL, e.g. alloc failed under pool
+	 * exhaustion) has no IP header to inspect; net_pkt_ip_data() would
+	 * deref NULL. Treat as not-bcast/mcast. */
+	if (net_pkt_is_empty(pkt)) {
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	if (net_ipv4_is_addr_bcast_raw(net_pkt_iface(pkt),
 				       NET_IPV4_HDR(pkt)->dst) ||
 	    net_ipv4_is_addr_mcast_raw(NET_IPV4_HDR(pkt)->dst)) {
@@ -477,6 +484,7 @@
 					       struct net_eth_addr *dst)
 {
 	if (net_pkt_family(pkt) == NET_AF_INET &&
+	    !net_pkt_is_empty(pkt) &&
 	    net_ipv4_is_addr_mcast_raw(NET_IPV4_HDR(pkt)->dst)) {
 		/* Multicast address */
 		net_eth_ipv4_mcast_to_mac_addr(
@@ -532,6 +540,7 @@
 					       struct net_eth_addr *dst)
 {
 	if (net_pkt_family(pkt) == NET_AF_INET6 &&
+	    !net_pkt_is_empty(pkt) &&
 	    net_ipv6_is_addr_mcast_raw(NET_IPV6_HDR(pkt)->dst)) {
 		memcpy(dst, (uint8_t *)multicast_eth_addr.addr,
 		       sizeof(struct net_eth_addr) - 4);
